  "narrative": "Compared to last sale (10-29-26): Yearling cattle were too lightly tested to develop any market trend. Steer calves under 400 lbs were too lightly tested last week to develop an accurate market trend, however lower undertones were noticed. Steer calves 400-449 lbs sold mostly 20.00-30.00 lower; 450-549 lbs sold mostly 5.00 to 10.00 lower; steer calves 550-649 lbs sold unevenly steady from 5.00 higher to 10.00 lower; steer calves over 650 lbs sold sharply lower with most sales 20.00-25.00 lower. Heifer calves under 450 lbs were too lightly tested last week to develop an accurate market trend, however sharply lower undertones were noticed; Heifer calves 450-549 lbs sold steady to 10.00 lower; heifers over 550 lbs sold mostly 5.00-10.00 lower. Calves were offered in a variety of package sizes this week, but were mostly small to moderate with a couple of load lots seen. Quality this week was mixed from plain to very attractive. Very high quality cattle sold on very good demand this week, however plain to average quality cattle were met with mostly light demand. This led to wide price spreads at times. Many cut-back calves continue to be seen off summer video sales. Demand for light weight calves was significantly lighter this week as several buyers were off the market due wet pen conditions and lower CME positions. Rain fell early in the week and pen conditions at the yards were very muddy. Most cattle were dirty to very dirty as a result. A few offerings of weaned calves are starting to be seen. Many of these offerings were both very full and very dirty which limited demand for these offerings. CME positions have sold off sharply over the last few days, including today. Feeder cattle contracts sold with strong triple digit losses again today with most contracts 3.00 to 6.00 lower. Market activity was mostly active with a moderate to large size buying pool noticed. More buyers were present this week compared to last week. Billings livestock commission will not sale cows or bulls again this fall on Thursdays. Cows will be sold on Mondays during the fall run. Supply included: 100% Feeder Cattle (50% Steers, 47% Heifers, 2% Bulls). Feeder cattle supply over 600 lbs was 35%.",
